  "notes": "GAAP hospital (component unit of Polk County), entirely business-type; governmental fields null. Source statements: Statements of Financial Position (pp1-2), Statements of Revenues, Expenses and Changes in Net Position (p3), Statements of Cash Flows (p4; p5, added by the v7 re-trim, is its continuation: reconciliation of operating loss and supplemental disclosures, nothing new to record), Schedules 5-7 (pp6-9); 2025 column used. The statement of financial position is a single-entity statement, scope recorded as government-wide. Receipts = operating revenues (net patient service revenue, provision for bad debts, other revenue) plus nonoperating revenue lines; interest expense (28,404) is shown inside the printed 'Total nonoperating revenues' 643,947, but is recorded as a disbursement, so the receipts total 10,238,258 and disbursements total 9,720,999 are computed (excess 517,259 as printed). Capital grants and contributions 173,676 go in business_type.other_financing; net position 11,222,503 + 517,259 + 173,676 = 11,913,438. Schedule 5 gross charges by department were recorded using the Total column (Inpatient + Outpatient), with charity care and contractual adjustments as negative lines; they add to net patient service revenue 9,722,752. Schedule 7 expense detail recorded as two items per department line (Salaries and Wages; Supplies and Other, shown only when not a dash); total 8,906,429 differs from statement operating expenses less depreciation (8,915,898) by 9,469 as printed in the report (schedule excludes depreciation and employee benefits are inside Supplies and Other); recorded in report_discrepancies (salaries tie exactly; the Supplies and Other column is 9,469 short). Estimated third-party payor settlements asset categorized as other assets, liability as other liabilities. Read pages 1-9 of 9",
  "report_discrepancies": [
    {
      "check": "detail",
      "difference": -9469,
      "source_page": 9,
      "note": "Schedule 7 expense Totals 8,906,429 (salaries 4,034,745 + supplies and other 4,871,684) vs statement operating expenses less depreciation 8,915,898 (p3: salaries 4,034,745 + benefits 1,221,678 + supplies and other 3,659,475); Supplies and other column is 9,469 short as printed (2024 column also short by 10,533)."
    }
  ]
